@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Unlock prices and invoices";
}

<h1>Unlock prices and invoices</h1>

<p class="lead"><strong>Applies to:</strong> organisations on a <strong>Microsoft Customer
Agreement</strong>. If you bought online before 2023 you may still be on the older agreement; it
moves automatically at your next renewal.</p>

<p>
    <strong>Not sure which agreement you have?</strong> If MLCP says it cannot see your agreement
    yet, granting billing read access is how we find out. If you turn out to be on the older
    agreement, you can enter seat prices yourself meanwhile.
</p>

<p><strong>Who can do this:</strong> a <strong>Billing account owner</strong>. On a Microsoft
Customer Agreement, a Global Administrator can make themselves one: Azure portal &rarr;
<em>Cost Management + Billing &rarr; Billing scopes</em> &rarr; select the billing account &rarr;
<em>Access control (IAM)</em> &rarr; <em>Elevate access</em>.</p>

<div class="alert alert-info" role="note">
    <strong>Why a third step.</strong> Billing permissions are separate from both app consent and
    Azure resource permissions. You can complete both of those and still see no prices. We need
    read-only access to your billing account.
</div>

<h2 class="h5">Steps</h2>
<ol>
    <li>Azure portal &rarr; <strong>Cost Management + Billing</strong> &rarr;
        <strong>Billing scopes</strong> &rarr; select your billing account.</li>
    <li><strong>Access control (IAM) &rarr; Add</strong>.</li>
    <li>Role: <strong>Billing account reader</strong>, for prices, subscriptions and renewals.</li>
    <li>Member: search <strong>MLCP</strong> &rarr; Add.</li>
    <li>For invoice downloads, also open <strong>Billing profiles</strong> &rarr; select each
        billing profile &rarr; <strong>Access control (IAM) &rarr; Add</strong> &rarr;
        <strong>Invoice manager</strong> &rarr; <strong>MLCP</strong>. Invoice manager is a
        billing <em>profile</em> role, so it is granted on each profile, not on the account.</li>
</ol>

<h2 class="h5">What this unlocks</h2>
<ul>
    <li>The per-seat prices you actually pay, not list prices</li>
    <li>Monthly invoices, downloaded on demand and never stored by us</li>
    <li>Auto-renew status and term end dates</li>
    <li>Azure purchases such as reservations, and faster cost reading</li>
</ul>

